//===----------------------------------------------------------------------===//
// The other half of `numa_tile_larger_than_one_node.vx`: a tile that fits one
// NUMA node is admitted, and the hop to the other node is priced rather than
// merely permitted.
//
// 8 GiB staged into node0 and then moved to node1. Both routes resolve, and the
// second is the more expensive one -- 68 GB/s to reach a node's own memory
// against 38 GB/s across the interconnect, so the model predicts the remote hop
// costs about 1.8x the local one for the same bytes.
//
// That ratio is the point of the file. A capacity check alone would say the far
// node is just more room; what makes it a *different* space is that reaching it
// costs something reaching local memory does not, and a number that says so is
// what an experiment can go and falsify. Both figures are UNVERIFIED -- see
// fleet/xeon-e5-2666v3.vx, which derives them and says so.
//
// The costs are asserted in picoseconds against 8 GiB, so they move if either
// declared rate does. That is deliberate: this file should fail the day a
// measurement replaces a derivation, and the new number should be written here.
//
// The last two checks are about the other end. Each node's placement carries its
// own `target_topology` id into the emitted module, so the backend can tell the
// two apart -- which is what a runtime would need to bind an allocation to the
// right node. Nothing decodes these yet; the ids being distinct is the part that
// has to be true before anything can.
//
// RUN: vxc %s --host default --machine fleet/xeon-e5-2666v3.vx --action emit-mlir -o /dev/null --diagnostics-json 2>/dev/null | FileCheck %s
// CHECK: "verdict": "admitted"
// CHECK: "path": ["CPU_DRAM", "HBM"]
// CHECK-SAME: "derived_cost": 126322567530
// CHECK: "path": ["HBM", "PEER_HBM"]
// CHECK-SAME: "derived_cost": 226050910316
// CHECK: vx.transfer
// CHECK-SAME: target_topology = 1855308478
// CHECK-SAME: space = "HBM"
// CHECK: vx.transfer
// CHECK-SAME: target_topology = 489426827
// CHECK-SAME: space = "PEER_HBM"

fn main() -> i32 {
  // 2097152 x 1024 x 4 B = 8 GiB, which fits either 30 GiB node.
  let t : Tensor<f32, [2097152, 1024]> = Tensor<f32, [2097152, 1024]>::uninit();
  let local = transfer(t, Memory::HBM);
  let _remote = transfer(local, Memory::PEER_HBM);
  return 0;
}
